9)A school application wants to create a package studentInfo with class Student having method displayInfo(). Import and use it in another file.

STEPS TO CREATE

Create a folder named PackageDemo.
Create a subfolder named studentInfo.
Create Student.java inside the studentInfo folder.
Create Main.java inside the PackageDemo folder.
Import the Student class into Main.java.
Structure:
PackageDemo
│
├── Main.java
│
└── studentInfo
    ├── Student.java
    └── Student.class
Compile both Java files.
Execute the program and display the output:
PS C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\PackageDemo> javac studentInfo/Student.java
PS C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\PackageDemo> javac Main.java
PS C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\PackageDemo> java Main
Student Name: Yashaswini
Course: CSE

File 1: Student.java:code:
package studentInfo;

public class Student {
    public void displayInfo() {
        System.out.println("Student Name: Yashaswini");
        System.out.println("Course: CSE");
    }
}

File 2: Main.java:code:
import studentInfo.Student;

public class Main9 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s = new Student();
        s.displayInfo();
    }
}
